                <div class="mb-5" id="faq">
                    <h3>Frequently Asked Questions</h3>
                    <h5 class="mt-2">1. Which are the top universities in Finland for international students?</h5>
                    <p>
                        Some of the top universities in Finland include Aalto University, the University of Helsinki,
                        Tampere University, LUT University, the University of Oulu, and the University of Turku.
                        These institutions are recognized for academic excellence, research opportunities, and strong
                        industry connections.
                    </p>

                    <h5>2. Which university in Finland is best for Indian students?</h5>
                    <p>
                        The best university depends on your course and career goals. Aalto University is highly
                        regarded for engineering and technology, while the University of Helsinki is known for research
                        and academic excellence. Business students often prefer Hanken School of Economics.
                    </p>

                    <h5>3. What is the average tuition fee at top universities in Finland?</h5>
                    <p>
                        Tuition fees for international students typically range from €6,000 to €18,000 per year,
                        depending on the university and study program. Many universities also offer merit-based
                        scholarships to reduce tuition costs.
                    </p>

                    <h5>4. Can Indian students get scholarships at Finnish universities?</h5>
                    <p>
                        Yes, most Finnish universities offer scholarships for international students. These may include
                        partial tuition waivers, full tuition fee scholarships, or academic merit-based awards.
                    </p>

